                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4a48ad68-02a7-3887-8743-0df6096536a3",
                        "entry_id": "ef9dccdc-594a-3fbe-bb8f-6ab1438c576d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "staatenähnliches Gebilde, welches wie ein eigenständiger Staat auftritt, aber nach dem Völkerrecht keiner ist"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d60e5537-6212-4789-a783-8572a9bfdf7a",
                                "sense_id": "4a48ad68-02a7-3887-8743-0df6096536a3",
                                "text": "Er ist \"informeller Hobby-Außenminister\" der Mikronation Bunte Republik Neustadt (BRN), die Anspruch auf einen reichlichen Quadratkilometer erhebt, der in den Grenzen von Dresdens hübschem Gründerzeitviertel Äußere Neustadt liegt."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6ebf7c6d-a7d2-4202-a67e-eabf65958ab4",
                        "source_entry_id": "ef9dccdc-594a-3fbe-bb8f-6ab1438c576d",
                        "source_sense_id": "4a48ad68-02a7-3887-8743-0df6096536a3",
                        "target_lang_word": "micronation",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "micronation",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7c779242-2e2d-3866-897f-3e66b737611d",
                                        "entry_id": "9eb76ff8-a4a0-39ed-8b94-91a60357759c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A non-autonomous entity that claims to be a sovereign state and mimics the actions of a state (with varying degrees of seriousness), but lacks any legal recognition and exists only on paper or in the mind of its creator; a micronational entity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "57d6a12b-23b9-4681-8680-ea89091ac6d9",
                                                "sense_id": "7c779242-2e2d-3866-897f-3e66b737611d",
                                                "text": "For every dreamer there is somewhere a doer, and in the realm [of] the strange micro-nations, the Republic of Minerva has plunged a bit ahead of the nebulous status of most others."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "82a21ac2-e3ec-4782-aaab-163a20e8ecd4",
                                                "sense_id": "7c779242-2e2d-3866-897f-3e66b737611d",
                                                "text": "Oceanus ... This is the world's largest micronation, taking up all the seas of the world beyond national 3-mi. limits."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "526d1457-2f35-4360-854d-b704e5845a50",
                                                "sense_id": "7c779242-2e2d-3866-897f-3e66b737611d",
                                                "text": "The list of micro-nations is long and colorful. The spirit of new nation-building that resonates from King Robert's descriptions of these countries, is seductive."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0c3e784e-a5d4-43dc-80f1-db9e70e90837",
                                                "sense_id": "7c779242-2e2d-3866-897f-3e66b737611d",
                                                "text": "Even if you are very well traveled, you may not yet have visited any of the world's micronations. There are places all over where someone or some group has declared a sort of mock sovereignty. Real nations mostly ignore them, and so does everyone else usually."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "11df7257-ca6a-45c7-be5a-0829cb84fa52",
                                                "sense_id": "7c779242-2e2d-3866-897f-3e66b737611d",
                                                "text": "[Never heard of] the Imperial Kingdom of Calsahara? The Conch Republic? The Principality of Sealand? You’re not alone. Léo Delafontaine hadn’t either until 2012, when he visited the Republic of Saugeais, a self-proclaimed micronation in eastern France. He's since become fascinated with \"countries\" unrecognized by world governments and organizations. […] Some micronations are easily accessible while others are difficult to get to."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0175ea83-d0b8-48c3-9862-830ab03cc070",
                                                "sense_id": "7c779242-2e2d-3866-897f-3e66b737611d",
                                                "text": "After exploring several classificatory accounts that identify commonalities and distinctions among and between different types of micronation, we outline our definition. We find that micronations are self-declared nations that perform and mimic acts of sovereignty, and adopt many of the protocols of nations, but lack a foundation in domestic and international law for their existence and are not recognised as states in domestic or international forums."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "26e98e33-b5bf-3455-a878-a3b8ba4f2369",
                                        "entry_id": "9eb76ff8-a4a0-39ed-8b94-91a60357759c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of microstate (“a country that has a very small population and land area”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "898255e8-3aa8-44da-a328-01ab0d304e97",
                                                "sense_id": "26e98e33-b5bf-3455-a878-a3b8ba4f2369",
                                                "text": "Also, since Nigeria is the cornerstone of the economy of West Africa, many countries around its perimeter will suffer, including many of the \"micro-nations\" of the U.N. which were the biggest supporters of the actions in The Congo and Rhodesia."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "097e46fa-1a31-4ad3-a216-bcd7ec32db07",
                                                "sense_id": "26e98e33-b5bf-3455-a878-a3b8ba4f2369",
                                                "text": "The concept of an independent Bougainville is sometimes denounced because such a micronation would necessarily restrict the scope of employment opportunities while increasing the frustrations of educated Bougainvilleans."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c90f9c46-c978-4fd9-8766-715ece834fed",
                                                "sense_id": "26e98e33-b5bf-3455-a878-a3b8ba4f2369",
                                                "text": "Europe already has workable arrangements with micro-nations like Luxembourg, Liechtenstein, Andorra and San Marino."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0b700330-7115-46c9-bf7a-3001270c078c",
                                                "sense_id": "26e98e33-b5bf-3455-a878-a3b8ba4f2369",
                                                "text": "But in easing its own vaccine crisis, this hilltop micronation – which is not a member of the European Union – has become a foil for a much larger crisis playing out beyond its borders."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "micronation",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d335a483-b328-344d-b3fe-819a32ef75ec",
                                        "entry_id": "af5296f9-9499-3648-b662-4e28ba234a70",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A small nation (“historically constituted, stable community of people, formed based on a common language, territory, economic life, ethnicity and manifested in a common culture”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncommon"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "96b5270c-a2b7-43e3-8682-1f9860fed113",
                                                "sense_id": "d335a483-b328-344d-b3fe-819a32ef75ec",
                                                "text": "Careful groundwork had given Germany a highly unified micronation within the boundaries of Argentina, in many ways better prepared and better organized than the Argentine nation itself."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aab64e7e-9812-497c-a025-263c261e4631",
                                                "sense_id": "d335a483-b328-344d-b3fe-819a32ef75ec",
                                                "text": "We are faced with micronationalisms that need be tamed, micronations that will have to be organized."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fadadf92-29cf-40cd-a055-e113fa7382ac",
                                                "sense_id": "d335a483-b328-344d-b3fe-819a32ef75ec",
                                                "text": "Margery Perham once remarked that white Rhodesia was a micronation equivalent to a medium-sized British town. How has this micronation, about 80 per cent of whom live in the urban areas, been able to develop and retain control over the African population for so long?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "10a60691-8b38-4abc-9eca-dd31216da8b2",
                                                "sense_id": "d335a483-b328-344d-b3fe-819a32ef75ec",
                                                "text": "Leaving aside micro-nations, the Soviet Union is a large Slavic nation state to which are attached some reluctant Europeans in the west."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c66a96cc-303d-4461-83a3-0fc4457490ce",
                        "source_entry_id": "ef9dccdc-594a-3fbe-bb8f-6ab1438c576d",
                        "source_sense_id": "4a48ad68-02a7-3887-8743-0df6096536a3",
                        "target_lang_word": "micronation",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "micronation",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4563c4b9-982f-3bc7-9dab-28d43ed78a92",
                                        "entry_id": "a68702ea-72f7-34da-bd2f-251ef632b04b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Nation indépendante créée par un petit nombre de personnes, sans reconnaissance des autorités internationales."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ab3bc4a-5248-4b97-9ae8-38f9366f05bd",
                                                "sense_id": "4563c4b9-982f-3bc7-9dab-28d43ed78a92",
                                                "text": "Ce n’était pas la première fois qu’une micronation entamait une procédure de reconnaissance avec le Somaliland."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
